{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792446650,"nonce":"6/Y6hj2rbrrdG85aGaqjRQrr7X0=","message":"Inactive code tabs now retain document data, not editor instances\n\nAshui commit 3f1b3e5cb38deca9d381470c644c8dd289f34d06 introduces CodeEditorState: shared text, bounded CodeHistory, syntax/fold and annotation caches, and selection/scroll. The mounted view alone owns TextEditing, measured rows, reactive watches, minimap and native controls. Its capture hook is cleared on disposal, with generation handling for replacement before old-view cleanup. RayDE pins this commit and mounts code views only for the active file, including extension source panes.\n\nClosed saved documents, buffers and empty editor refs are evicted. Closed unsaved text/history survives reopening and is released after saving. Live development/theme buffers remain available. Renames carry the document state to the new path. Scroll-rest timers are cancelled and their editor reference cleared on unmount; delayed breakpoint synchronization reads document annotations rather than needing a mounted view.\n\nSame dark ten-tab + Git workload, old pin e1b0a70 versus new state implementation (physical footprint from vmmap, not hl.Gc.currentMemory): baseline 149.7 -\u003e 150.4 MiB; open-tabs-collected 695.3 -\u003e 495.2 MiB; gpu-drained after closing 409.6 -\u003e 327.9 MiB. At open-tabs-collected, live CodeEditors 10 -\u003e 0 (Git history active), watches 7740 -\u003e 741, canvases 13 -\u003e 3, layout nodes 1255 -\u003e 365. Ten document caches remain, 818 characters / 62 lines, no mounted documents/minimaps. Across all 70 new checkpoints, at most one code editor is live, with zero disposed component hosts. Closing all files leaves zero documents/editors/canvases. This reduces inactive-view retention; remaining post-close footprint is still open.\n\nValidation: Ashui CodeComponents 266 checks and CodeStateLifecycle 20 checks pass. RayDE Basic, Git, Full, Assist, Debug, Theme Studio and Documents scenarios pass in both schemes, including undo/redo after unmount, selection/folds/scroll, clean cache eviction and dirty-close/save/reopen. Snapshots are under bin/editor-state-snapshots. Existing Git assertions now expect retained document identity and a remounted editor/minimap, while keeping stable tab headers. Native ordinary-file lifecycle passes both normally and with ASH_GC_DEBUG_ROOTS=1 ASH_GC_STATS=1; final editor/document/canvas counts are zero.\n\nLarge-file profiling exposed a separate existing Problems-panel null access: a compiler command-line diagnostic can have neither file nor range. The source-copy fixture produces such an error because its package differs from the fixture path. The panel now displays Workspace and does not navigate for location-less diagnostics; both-theme snapshots cover that case. The large Workbench.hx open/close probe now passes with both GC flags, ending with zero cached documents/editors/canvases. The original failed probe logs were retained for diagnosis; the successful large-file log is bin/interaction-document-state-large-hl/run.log.\n\nMeasurements: bin/interaction-document-state/results.json and vmmap summaries; native small-file GC log: bin/interaction-document-state-roots-native/run.log. Native executable and macOS package are rebuilt for preview. The new pin reuses the existing identical native library/CSS compiler cache; no new Cargo target or worktree was created.","files":null}]}